        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles Laughton, Fredric March, Frances Drake, Elsa Lanchester, Victor Hugo\n- Works: Les Misérables, Les Misérables (1935 film)\n- Topics: film adaptation, marriage, acting careers\n\nFacts:\n- In 1927, Charles Laughton was cast in a play with his future wife Elsa Lanchester.\n- Charles Laughton lived and worked with Elsa Lanchester until his death, and they had no children.\n- Les Misérables is a 1935 American drama film based on Victor Hugo's novel Les Misérables.\n- Les Misérables stars Fredric March and Charles Laughton.\n- Frances Drake was an American actress born on October 22, 1912, and she was best known for playing Eponine in Les Misérables (1935).\n- Frances Drake died on January 18, 2000.",
